# Day 12

**23km / 5 hours**

"It rained and rained and rained and rained" is how a well known New Zealand tramping poem starts and it felt very apposite today. It started in clear weather but soon there was some light drizzle. Not to worry but soon it became harder until at one point being quite heavy. The track itself was mostly road, whether the highway or logging roads so not that special except there may have been great views to see on a fine day.

![The incredible views I could see of the stunning beaches in the Bay of Islands](./gloomy-day.jpg)

Not to worry, rain is a part of tramping in NZ and this wasn't such a bad day for it, it wasn't a muddy track and even though it was less pleasant, it's all manageable. We were planning to kayak tomorrow but the poor weather may have prevented that so may need to just ferry and walk as per the standard route. It is what it is.

In Paihia it fined up so I could do some more shopping and sitting next to the beach thinking about things. I do intend to do more blog posts about things that aren't just the day to day logs but there's always things occupying the time.